WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:04.830
Bloopers offer a peek into the filmmaking
process, humanizing Hollywood stars by showing

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:09.010
them flubbing their lines, goofing up, and
just generally having a good, silly time while

00:00:09.010 --> 00:00:10.440
it's all captured for posterity.

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:15.320
Bloopers are especially fun when they're from
unexpected sources—such as serious actors

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:17.120
who win lots of awards for their dramatic
roles.

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:22.480
Here are some little-seen screw-ups and goof-offs
from some of the most respected dramatic performers

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:23.400
in Hollywood history.

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:25.260
Marlon Brando

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:30.640
Among the most acclaimed actors of all time,
Marlon Brando disappeared into his characters

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:33.340
in classic films like The Godfather and On
the Waterfront.

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:38.700
He lends just the right amount of gravitas
to the role of Superman's father in a cameo

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:41.340
appearance in the first Superman film in 1978.

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:47.060
But while Brando was once the very definition
of "serious actor," he didn't always take

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:48.620
himself all that seriously.

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:52.700
In one outtake from Superman, he transitions
from the scripted poem ...

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:57.040
"A tree whose branches wide and strong…"

00:00:57.720 --> 00:01:01.020
… into a Stephen Foster song, cracking up
the crew ...

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:08.060
" … the Camptown ladies sing this song / Doo
dah / Doo dah … "

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:09.300
"Cut!"

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:11.240
Hugh Jackman

00:01:12.460 --> 00:01:17.460
A versatile actor equally skilled to handle
costume dramas, action movies, and musicals,

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:21.850
Hugh Jackman is best known for the role of
Wolverine in the X-Men series, and brings

00:01:21.850 --> 00:01:25.500
depth and nuance to a comic book character
that could be one-note.

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:30.640
But on the set of the 2004 monster-hunter
movie Van Helsing, he doesn't even have Wolverine's

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:34.100
adamantium claws to blame for a prop breaking
in his hands ...

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:36.800
"Hmmm.

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:37.800
Broke.

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:40.660
Good enough.

00:01:40.760 --> 00:01:41.580
It's a low-budget movie!

00:01:42.020 --> 00:01:42.600
I'm sorry!"

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:44.220
Bryan Cranston

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:50.300
As Walter White on Breaking Bad, Bryan Cranston
was the ominous "one who knocks"—and he

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:52.550
won four Emmys for his gripping portrayal.

00:01:52.550 --> 00:01:58.119
That role involved a lot of difficult dialogue,
from long monologues to rattling off the names

00:01:58.120 --> 00:02:00.260
of chemicals and scientific processes.

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:06.160
But it didn't prepare Cranston for one particularly
gnarly bit of dialogue in the 2012 remake

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:07.160
of Total Recall ...

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:11.640
"I want him alive for re — re-implantation."

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:14.680
BOOP
"I want him alive for re-inflan —" BOOP

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:16.040
"Re-implantation."

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:17.900
Naomi Watts

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:24.600
While she almost exclusively acts in really
intense dramas like 21 Grams and The Impossible,

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:29.100
Naomi Watts lightened her workload a little
with a major role in Peter Jackson's King

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:30.900
Kong remake in 2005.

00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:36.560
The blooper reel for the movie reveals an
actress that has an almost pathological inclination

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:38.160
to swear when she flubs a line ...

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:40.080
"Is it — oh, for f---'s sake."

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:48.020
"The thing that I was afraid of is that you
would be one of those self-obsessed … f---wits."

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:49.300
Matt Damon

00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:54.710
He's one of the finest actors of his generation,
and a beloved movie star to boot, but Matt

00:02:54.710 --> 00:02:59.880
Damon, of course, is not really a genius scientist—he
just plays one in The Martian.

00:03:00.220 --> 00:03:05.080
Most of Damon's scenes in the sci-fi film
are of him alone, stranded on Mars, carefully

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:07.860
devising ways that he can prolong his survival.

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:13.300
Math helps in that kind of situation, but
Damon amusingly had a hard time getting that

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:14.300
part right ...

00:03:19.580 --> 00:03:20.660
"Oh Jesus."

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:23.960
"Let's clean that up and go again please."

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:25.060
Uma Thurman

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:31.720
As the stoic, revenge-obsessed Bride in Quentin
Tarantino's two-part Kill Bill epic, Uma Thurman

00:03:31.740 --> 00:03:33.400
rarely got a chance to be funny.

00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:38.720
Her character is generally about as hilarious
as a hole in the head…like the one Thurman

00:03:38.740 --> 00:03:42.959
makes when she reaches into a fight opponent's
noggin and pulls out a bloody eyeball ...

00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:46.200
"And … action!"

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:49.700
"Cut!"

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:52.680
"Oh, c'mon, let's do it again!"

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:54.020
J.K. Simmons

00:03:55.080 --> 00:03:59.900
One of the most prolific and versatile character
actors in Hollywood, J.K. Simmons won an Oscar

00:03:59.910 --> 00:04:05.280
for his role as a brutal drum instructor in
Whiplash… which was a far cry from his role

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:11.140
as a soft-spoken police chief on the TNT cop
drama The Closer… which is a far cry from

00:04:11.140 --> 00:04:16.240
his role as the blustery newspaper editor
J. Jonah Jameson in the first Spider-Man trilogy.

00:04:16.769 --> 00:04:21.960
He's got to deliver Jameson's lines strongly,
loudly, and at a rapid clip — in an outtake

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:25.200
from Spider-Man 3, Simmons gets at least two
out of three right ...

00:04:25.960 --> 00:04:28.460
"Congratulations, son ... (unintelligible
gibberish).

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:32.440
"Congratulations, Brock, we'll use your shot
… (unintelligible gibberish)."

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:34.040
Thanks for watching!

00:04:34.360 --> 00:04:36.820
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:36.830 --> 00:04:38.910
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

